fix(pipeline-lab): see the emulator's document-size error as production does

- map the emulator's 'maximum entity size' wording to the product's size_error, so
  log_largest_write and the size backoff run as in production;
- keep the product's size warning (kind and bytes only) on the failing driver event;
- planpass passes silence_gap to planner.windows for #25794 refs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

fix(pipeline-lab): a real v3 day completes; batched seeding, reproducible reset, merged status

The first real-day dry run failed in seeding after 198 s. Fixes, each with a synthetic test:
- conversations seed through the product's encode seam in batches (not the per-row processing
  upsert); per-row failures become counted run warnings, never silent drops;
- blobs still sealed under the production key (open_loop_extractions) are cleared and counted;
- memory ledger commits over Firestore's entity limit are split until they fit;
- a focused goal is created in the background, then focused;
- a down Typesense turns the product's index-write kill switch on (decision typesense_unavailable);
- the reset also clears the lab uid's top-level docs and Redis keys (finalization jobs and
  daily-summary locks made a re-run take other paths), keeping the batch privacy authority;
- v3 production rows sharing recordings with a replay conversation are "merged", not "missing";
- the stage cache key carries the selected pipeline; phase and seed timings in chain_entry.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
